%N A399933 Maximum number of Hamiltonian cycles in a polyiamond with 2*n cells.
%C A399933 The cycles pass from a cell to a neighboring cell, visiting each cell exactly once.
%C A399933 We follow the convention that K_2 has 1 Hamiltonian cycle, so a(1) = 1.
%H A399933 Pontus von Brömssen, <a href="/A399933/a399933.svg">Illustration of all (free) polyiamonds with 2*n = 38..42 cells and a(n) = 2 Hamiltonian cycles</a>. (A cycle consists of the black edges together with either the red or the blue edges.)
%H A399933 <a href="/index/Pol#polyominoes">Index entries for sequences related to polyominoes</a>.
